<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>Today.</h2>
<div>
<p class="nm-page-copy">My current territory is <a href="ai-media.html">AI-native media</a>: products and operations designed with AI inside the workflow rather than bolted onto the output. It grows out of earlier work in media, product, marketing, content, audiences, and communities. I build and test agents, research systems, live-production tools, editorial infrastructure, product experiments, and small interfaces that make difficult operational work more legible.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">I also write <a href="essays.html">Narrative Mechanics</a>, a body of essays and frameworks about positioning, attention, trust, product meaning, and what changes when machines increasingly mediate discovery.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>The foundation.</h2>
<div class="nm-ledger"> <a href="work.html"><span class="nm-page-label">Digital media</span><strong>Companies, formats, and operating systems</strong><p>Podcasting, digital publishing, live production, distributed teams, and the machinery behind continuous media.</p></a> <a href="about.html#products"><span class="nm-page-label">Digital products</span><strong>Audience-facing experiences and internal tools</strong><p>Product strategy, interfaces, workflows, feedback loops, and practical tools built around real constraints.</p></a> <a href="work-posta.html"><span class="nm-page-label">Marketing and distribution</span><strong>Helping a format become legible and find demand</strong><p>Positioning, growth, brand relationships, channel design, and distribution when the market category is still forming.</p></a> <a href="essays.html"><span class="nm-page-label">Content strategy</span><strong>Programming, branded content, editorial systems, and narrative</strong><p>Content as part of a product and operating model, not an isolated stream of output.</p></a> <a href="zmox.html"><span class="nm-page-label">Audiences and communities</span><strong>From reach and return to participation and shared language</strong><p>Audience development, feedback, trust, community dynamics, and the difference between attention and belonging.</p></a> </div>
